# Every Podman secret an Accounted instance needs, and how it is made.
#   <name> <kind> [arg]
# kinds:
#   hex N         N random bytes, hex-encoded (2N characters)
#   jwt ROLE      HS256 JWT for ROLE, signed with accounted-jwt-secret (Supabase anon / service_role keys)
#   supplied      a value a person provides once via --from <0600 file>; optional until a unit needs it
# Reconciled with upstream self-hosted/v0.8.4 .env.example (2026-11-17). Not made: the opaque
# publishable/secret keys and asymmetric JWT_KEYS (optional upstream; Accounted uses the HS256
# anon/service_role keys), VAULT_ENC_KEY (Supavisor only, dropped), LOGFLARE_* (logs overlay, unused).
accounted-jwt-secret               hex 32
accounted-anon-key                 jwt anon
accounted-service-role-key         jwt service_role
accounted-postgres-password        hex 32
accounted-cron-secret              hex 32
accounted-realtime-secret-key-base hex 48
accounted-realtime-db-enc-key      hex 8
accounted-pg-meta-crypto-key       hex 16
accounted-dashboard-password       hex 16
accounted-s3-protocol-key-id       hex 16
accounted-s3-protocol-key-secret   hex 32
accounted-smtp-password            supplied
